  "description": "kubectl-why-fail diagnoses a failing pod and explains the cause in plain\nlanguage instead of raw kubectl describe/events/logs output. It covers\nthe ten most common failure modes (CrashLoopBackOff, OOMKilled,\nImagePullBackOff, stuck PVCs, and more) with deterministic, fully\ntested rules that answer instantly with no network calls. An optional\nAI fallback (your own free OpenRouter API key) covers rarer cases.\n",
